  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-11-09T14:07:24.962Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As a creator, I want to be able to block specific players from using my public avatars or visiting my uploaded worlds.\n\nRight now, even if we block or report someone, they can still join our public worlds or wear our avatars, which makes it impossible to protect ourselves and our communities from targeted harassment or organized trolling. When a group of such players repeatedly invades a world, there’s no fast or effective way to stop them — even the vote-kick and group block systems are not enough.\n\nA “Creator Block List” feature would allow creators to deny access to specific users across all of their content. This would greatly improve safety for both creators and players, without affecting normal social interactions.\n\nPossible implementation ideas:\n\n- Blocked users cannot spawn or equip avatars made by that creator.\n\n- Blocked users cannot join any instances of that creator’s worlds (unless invited).\n\n- The block list could be managed through the VRChat website or SDK.\n\nPlease give creators the tools they need to protect their spaces. This is not about limiting freedom — it’s about ensuring a safe and respectful environment for everyone.",
